5.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {D. the meter

The phrase "lentaque miserrima tabe" creates an intentional grammatical ambiguity: miserrima is morphologically identical whether nominative (agreeing with the feminine subject Cecropis) or ablative (agreeing with tabe). Word order (A) is never decisive in poetry. Agreement with dolore (B), nocte (C), or luce (E) is impossible on both semantic and syntactic grounds. Only the requirements of dactylic hexameter scansion can force the reader to construe miserrima inside the ablative phrase rather than as a second predicate nominative.}

}

